dosa 0002
  kala: 2026-08-20T09:51:01Z
  karta: cf-dosalekha
  jati: karana-dosa
  vastu: machine/MathMachine.hs:2402-2406
  yatna: transport "agda checked this" from the checker to the engine's verdict, at the second call site, the one Certificate.hs's repair does not cover
  hetu: the site reads a process exit status and nothing else -- `case code of ExitSuccess -> KERNEL-ACCEPT` -- and an exit status is not evidence about mathematics.  There is no equivalence between "a process returned 0" and "the claim was proved"; the two sides are not the same object, so no transport exists to carry one to the other
  hetu: the repair for exactly this finding exists in the repository and does not reach here.  machine/Certificate.hs runs canaryTrue and canaryFalse through the same runAgda before honouring any acceptance; this call site runs neither
  nasta: machine/MathMachine.hs:2402-2406 -- readProcessWithExitCode "sh" ["-c", "cd formal/cubical && LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 agda " ++ modName ++ ".agda"] "" ; case code of ExitSuccess -> hPrintf logh "  KERNEL-ACCEPT ..." ; pure True
  nasta: the exhibited separation, from machine/GATE_AUDIT_DISPOSITION.md section 2: a shim reading `agda "$@" 2>&1 | cat` makes the pipeline's exit status its LAST stage's.  Real agda runs, really reports `suc x != x`, really exits 1 -- and the gate read 0 and returned Certified "refl" 1 for s(x) = x
  nasta: the same audit's third route: machine/.certcache is an unauthenticated directory, and one hand-written file turned s(x) = x into a Certified for ZERO agda invocations (GateAudit --probe poison)
  nasta: what a collapse here destroys is the distinction between MATHEMATICALLY REFUSED and ENVIRONMENTALLY BROKEN: the 2026-08-15 fault in which every candidate became a KERNEL-REJECT because the include root had moved is indistinguishable, at this site, from a corpus of false candidates
  yogyata-drsta: machine/MathMachine.hs lines 2380-2412 read in full; machine/Certificate.hs (canaryTrue/canaryFalse at 247-248, 832-836); machine/GATE_AUDIT_DISPOSITION.md sections 2 and 3
  yogyata-ksetra: the two agda-invoking call sites in machine/MathMachine.hs.  Not a survey of every agda invocation in the repository
  yogyata-avadhi: NO claim that this site has ever been fooled in a real run, and none that the environment is currently broken.  The claim is only that the site cannot tell the two apart, which is a property of the code and is exhibited above
  sesa: the audit's own asymmetry, handed forward: a wrong rejection costs a theorem, a wrong acceptance installs a false rewrite rule that every later round reasons with.  So this site's exposure is not symmetric and the canary belongs on the accepting branch
  pramana: machine/GATE_AUDIT_DISPOSITION.md, 2026-08-16, findings 1-4 and L1-L2 with their dispositions
  pramana: Nyaya on pramana: what arrives by an unaccepted route is not weak evidence, it is apramana, and apramana does not accumulate (AHIMSA_SUTRA_VISTARA section 19)
  punarabhinaya: sed -n '2400,2410p' machine/MathMachine.hs
